  "notes": "REQ-2.3.3 extends REQ-2.3.1/REQ-2.3.2: deleting a note now soft-deletes it server-side (deleted=true, deletedAt=now) so it lands in the Trash view instead of being removed permanently. Clicking the Trash item in the sidebar opens the trash view: a 'Trash' heading, the list of deleted notes, and an 'Empty trash' button that permanently removes all deleted notes (DELETE /api/trash). Deleted notes are automatically purged after seven days (server purge on startup and when reading/emptying trash). The Undo flow from REQ-2.3.2 still restores the note (POST /api/notes with the original id/timestamps, cleared deleted flag), and the REQ-2.3.2 toast texts ('Note deleted', 'Action undone') are unchanged. Seed contains the deletable regular note 'Delete me 2.3.3' plus the REQ-2.3.1/REQ-2.3.2 dependency notes."
